handoff:

The delegation convention in 18 says a subagent claims with PIDLY_AGENT and a
lease, because a subagent shares its parent's process — a Bash call from a
subagent reports the same CLAUDE_PID as the lead agent, so a pid cannot tell
them apart.

What was never checked is whether the harness gives a subagent a session
identifier of its own. One echo from inside a subagent settles it. If it is
distinct it is the natural PIDLY_AGENT value, and the convention gets a
generated name instead of one the lead agent has to invent and pass down.

The reference currently tells agents to make a name up:

  PIDLY_AGENT=sub-review-parser PIDLY_LEASE=1h pidly claim 19

Which works, and is one more thing for a prompt to get wrong.

Done when the answer is known, the reference says whichever is right, and
23 can rely on it rather than repeating the hand-written form.
